  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Scaling up of interventions to combat tuberculosis in Cote d?Ivoire - C&#xf4;te d&apos;Ivoire (01-Jan-2016-31-Dec-2017)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">C&#xf4;te d&apos;Ivoire, Tuberculosis, Alliance Nationale pour la Sant&#xe9; et le D&#xe9;veloppement en C&#xf4;te D&apos;Ivoire (Alliance C&#xf4;te d&apos;Ivoire)This program has the following goals: Reduce the TB mortality rate by 20 percent by 2020 compared with 2015.. The objectives of this program are: Achieve a treatment success rate of at least 86 percent by 2017.  Improve and strengthen the technical, management and coordination capacities of the National Tuberculosis Control Program (NTCP).  Increase notification of cases of all forms of TB (TBAF) from 23,750 in 2014 to 26,773 in 2017.  Increase the proportion of notified TB patients who are tested for HIV from 93 percent in 2014 to 100 percent in 2016 and increase the proportion of patients with TB/HIV treated using ARVs from 67 percent in 2013 to 90 percent in 2017..  Increase the treatment success rate from 56 percent of those MDR-TB patients treated in 2011 to 75 percent of those treated in 2017</narrative>
  </description>
